BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 619.0 Tm (1. A severe rise in intracranial pressure produces systemic hypertension with reflex bradycardia. What is) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 605.3 Tm (this response?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 588.6 Tm (Answer: D. Cushing reflex.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 572.3 Tm (Explanation: The Cushing response reflects brainstem ischaemia driving systemic hypertension, with) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 559.2 Tm (baroreflex-mediated bradycardia. Brain perfusion is threatened as raised intracranial pressure compresses cerebral) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 546.1 Tm (vessels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 530.0 Tm (Not A: Pulmonary hypoxic vasoconstriction is a local lung response.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 516.6 Tm (Not B: Atrial stretch does not explain raised ICP-driven hypertension.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 503.2 Tm (Not C: Bainbridge responds to increased atrial filling.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 489.8 Tm (Source: lecture-6:Q17 | 22-23) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 466.6 Tm (2. Which pressure relationship helps prevent fluid accumulation in normal pulmonary alveoli?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 449.9 Tm (Answer: C. Relatively low pulmonary capillary hydrostatic pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 433.6 Tm (Explanation: Low pulmonary capillary hydrostatic pressure relative to plasma oncotic forces helps minimise) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 420.5 Tm (filtration into air spaces.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 404.4 Tm (Not A: Pulmonary capillary pressure is much lower than systemic arterial pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 391.0 Tm (Not B: Plasma proteins contribute the inward oncotic force.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 377.6 Tm (Not D: Alveolar spaces normally contain little free fluid and protein.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 364.2 Tm (Source: lecture-6:Q32 | 31) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 341.0 Tm (3. A cuff that is far too small is used on a large upper arm. Which measurement error is likely?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 324.3 Tm (Answer: B. An undersized cuff gives a falsely high reading.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 308.0 Tm (Explanation: An undersized cuff transmits pressure poorly around a large arm and commonly overestimates measured) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 294.9 Tm (pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 278.8 Tm (Not A: Cuff size materially affects readings.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 265.4 Tm (Not C: Both systolic and diastolic measurements may be distorted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 252.0 Tm (Not D: A small cuff usually overestimates rather than underestimates BP.) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.2 Tf 0.43 0.45 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 238.6 Tm (Source: circulation-1:Q64 | 79-80; Chapter 10 ?8) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 215.4 Tm (4. The CSF volume is about 150 mL and production is 550 mL/day. Approximately how many complete turnovers) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.7 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 201.7 Tm (occur per day?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.3 Tf 0.1 0.33 0.58 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 185.0 Tm (Answer: A. About 4.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 168.7 Tm (Explanation: Dividing daily production by total CSF volume gives 550/150 ~ 3.7 turnovers each day.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 152.6 Tm (Not B: Two turnovers would require about 300 mL/day.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 139.2 Tm (Not C: One turnover would represent only about 150 mL/day.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.4 Tf 0.16 0.18 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 48.0 125.8 Tm (Not D: Six turnovers would correspond to around 900 mL/day.) Tj ET
